# Normalise line endings on commit.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF in the working copy, and the
# repository ends up storing whatever the last machine happened to use. Source files
# then show the entire file as changed the first time someone on Linux touches them.
#
# The rule: LF in the repository, always. Windows tooling that needs CRLF (batch
# files) is listed explicitly below.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch and PowerShell scripts must keep CRLF to run correctly.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.dat binary
*.ogg binary

# Generated lock files are text but should not be merged line-by-line.
gradle-wrapper.jar binary
